## Common Patterns

### API Service Pattern

```typescript
// services/resumeService.ts
import api from './api';
import { Resume, ResumeCreateRequest } from '../types/models';

export const createResume = async (data: ResumeCreateRequest): Promise<Resume> => {
  const response = await api.post<Resume>('/resumes', data);
  return response.data;
};
```

### Protected Route Pattern

```typescript
// Check auth in page components
const { user, loading } = useAuth();

if (loading) return <CircularProgress />;
if (!user) return <Navigate to="/login" />;
```

### Error Handling Pattern

```typescript
try {
  const result = await someApiCall();
  // handle success
} catch (error) {
  if (axios.isAxiosError(error)) {
    const message = error.response?.data?.detail || 'An error occurred';
    // show error to user
  }
}
```

---

## Key Data Models

Always refer to `src/types/models.ts` for the source of truth. Key interfaces:

- `User` - User account info
- `Profile` - User profile with personal info and preferences
- `Portfolio` - Skills, work experience, education, projects
- `Resume` - Generated resume with content sections
- `CoverLetter` - Generated cover letter linked to a resume
- `PortfolioWebsiteConfig` - Website deployment configuration

